# Onsen edition: the Magic Trackpad on the TP-Link UB500 goes quiet while its
# link is in sniff mode. bluez still says connected, the battery still reads,
# but touches never reach the host until something makes the kernel send Exit
# Sniff Mode. Only the controller's link policy can keep sniff off, and the
# kernel on this machine rejects the adapter-wide ioctl, so the policy is set
# per link, as soon as the trackpad's HID input device appears. uniq is the
# device's Bluetooth address.
#
# input[0-9]* only: the event node is a child with the same ancestry and would
# run the command a second time.
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="input", KERNEL=="input[0-9]*", ATTR{name}=="Apple Inc. Magic Trackpad", ATTR{uniq}=="?*", RUN+="/usr/bin/omarchy-bluetooth-link-policy $attr{uniq}"
